Fixed two race conditions in ``DataSet`` subscribers. A result inserted while a subscriber's
callback was running could be held back until the next insert, and when a dataset was
completed, its final callback could run concurrently with one already in progress on the
subscriber thread, delivering results out of order. Subscriber callbacks now never overlap
and always receive results in the order they were inserted. The length passed to a
subscriber callback is now always the number of results in the dataset up to and including
the ones passed along with it. Previously it could be off when results were inserted while
the callback was being called.
